    {
      "id": "claim_662ea9b9ec004cd98a9410f3d8b63ddd",
      "statement": "Offer establishment mints the RSA keypair exactly once at the top of generateOfferLink (before the peer exists), creates the RTCPeerConnection with a data channel (ordered:false) using the predicate-resolved ICE server, generates the local offer, then waits for ICE candidates to finish or a 3-second timeout (WAIT_ICE_CANDIDATES_TIMEOUT) before building the offer link; a per-invocation offerBuilt flag claims the build synchronously so the two paths build the link at most once and the timeout fallback can never rotate the key. Regeneration is generation-safe: before minting, generateOfferLink clears the pending ICE-candidate timer, nulls the handlers and closes the old data channel and RTCPeerConnection (unless already closed), resets the settled peer crypto (rsaPub to undefined, effectiveEncrypt re-pinned from the live setting) and the dead generation's UI state (new-file badge, isConnecting, pending answer code, and the dead generation's offer link so a failed regeneration returns to the clean generate state with no dead link to copy/QR/accept), and bumps a monotonically increasing offerGeneration token; the timeout fallback re-checks that token at fire time so a stale timer holding the previous generation's public key can never build a link from the new peer's SDP. Synchronous construction/offer-creation failures are caught and toasted instead of leaving the spinner stuck.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/OfferPage.svelte#L153-L298",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7a11bc4ceb10638bb8c77be56135fce9a8673054bcff824bce62ed87004fd724:"
        },
        {
