    {
      "id": "claim_168fa874ca494eb0b49c143450d46e27",
      "statement": "The answer peer decodes the attacker-controllable `s` URL param via sdpDecode (which throws synchronously on empty, invalid-base64, or non-SDP input) inside a try/catch that surfaces an 'Invalid SDP in link' toast instead of crashing the page during load (PR #45); the setOfferSDP promise is kept and awaited before createAnswer with a signalingState === 'have-remote-offer' check, so a rejected setRemoteDescription flips offerFailed and the UI renders an error state ('offer in the link is invalid') instead of the spinner spinning forever; it then awaits the validated p-param key import (a malformed key downgrades the session to plaintext) and produces the answer code sdpEncode(answerSdp) + '|' + base64(RSA public key) with the same 3-second ICE candidate timeout fallback.",
