    {
      "id": "claim_311d6dea83ac47ecbb8e7a3de45ee72a",
      "statement": "Both pages dispatch incoming data-channel messages through the shared handlePeerMessage helper in src/utils/peerMessage.ts (deduplicated from the two identical per-page handlers in PR #71): the same oneof switch (metaData routes to Receiver.onMetaData, chunk to Receiver.onChunkData, receiveEvent to Sender.onReceiveEvent), with Message.decode on the peer-controlled bytes wrapped in try/catch inside the helper so a malformed/truncated protobuf frame drops the frame and toasts 'Invalid message from peer' instead of crashing the page uncaught (PR #46). Both pages pin dataChannel.binaryType = 'arraybuffer' at channel acquisition (offer side at the createDataChannel site L119; answer side at the ondatachannel site L105) because WebRTC's default 'blob' would make new Uint8Array(Blob) zero-length and silently drop every frame (PR #95). Both pages additionally wire the data channel's onerror/onclose to sender?.onChannelClose() and receiver?.onChannelClose() so a dead channel marks in-flight/queued files 'connection lost' and stops their pipelines instead of leaking InvalidStateError into chunk pipelines (PR #74).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/OfferPage.svelte#L112-L155",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5ca82129b9fde9a60f628dae0b1ed60588b55cccce5a6bb0b2448500a6dc5dfb:"
