    {
      "id": "claim_3e6c7c1f906b402f9d8b244eea2dd87c",
      "statement": "The guarded data-channel send (dead-channel flag + readyState check + throwing-send catch) is a single shared helper: createChannelSender(dataChannel) in src/utils/channelSender.ts returns { send(message), isLost(), markLost() } — send no-ops with false when the lost flag is set or readyState !== 'open', returns true on success, and on a throwing send flips the lost flag and returns false instead of leaking InvalidStateError; markLost() is the idempotent flip fired by the owning component's onChannelClose(); isLost() is the live read both sides derive from. Sender.svelte and Receiver.svelte each create one instance and keep their call sites in the plain send(...) shape via destructuring (PR #97).",
